+// Rows [row0, row0 + rows) of one owner slice of the N-slice walk over the whole K: in0 is resident from tile-row 0
+// (later rows may still be tilizing behind it), the slice's weights sit in1_offset tiles past the weight CB front, and
+// the caller reserved the slice's pack region out_base tiles past the slice CB's write pointer (two streamed slices can
+// share one CB) and pushes it. Same math and pack as the walk's matmul_block call (Short init + INPUT_AND_OUTPUT
